## Quick start

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pip install -e .
pytest -q
```

## Run benchmark comparison

```bash
python -m performance_proxy.benchmark
```

This will generate a comparison between LRU and LFU policies and save a chart in the `results/` directory.

## Run synthetic load testing

```bash
python -m performance_proxy.load_test
```

## Example project summary for a resume

- Built a multithreaded HTTP proxy and caching layer in Python to evaluate request serving, eviction policies, and performance trade-offs under synthetic workloads.
- Implemented LRU and LFU cache replacement strategies and benchmarked hit rate and throughput across workload patterns, identifying workload-aware policy tradeoffs.
- Designed concurrency-safe request handling and synthetic load tests to measure latency and throughput under parallel access patterns.

## Notes

This project intentionally focuses on systems-level engineering fundamentals rather than a large external framework. It is particularly relevant for roles in systems, infrastructure, distributed systems, and performance engineering.
